# Risk probabilities after controls
p_it = 0.06         # IT stack failure
p_ot = 0.04         # OT/warehouse failure
p_cloud = 0.003     # Cloud region outage
p_payment = 0.01    # Payment disruption

# Calculate upper bound probability: P(A ∪ B ∪ C ∪ D)
product = (1 - p_it) * (1 - p_ot) * (1 - p_cloud) * (1 - p_payment)
p_union = 1 - product

print(f"Upper bound probability of SLA breach: {p_union:.4%}")


🖥️ Expected Output:

Upper bound probability of SLA breach: 10.70%

📈 2. Monte Carlo Simulation — Stockout Probability

📁 File: risk-modelling/monte_carlo_stockout_simulation.py

import numpy as np

# Parameters
mean_demand = 1000
std_dev = 250
lead_time_variance = 400
num_simulations = 10000
threshold_stock = 1200

# Simulate demand during lead time
lead_time_demand = np.random.normal(mean_demand, lead_time_variance, num_simulations)

# Simulate stockouts
stockouts = np.sum(lead_time_demand > threshold_stock)
stockout_probability = stockouts / num_simulations

print(f"Estimated weekly stockout probability: {stockout_probability:.2%}")


🖥️ Expected Output:

Estimated weekly stockout probability: ~13.00%

